VM Manager: resize the canvas when the server reactivates with another desktop size.

Hyper-V VMConnect accepts the requested size, then reactivates the session with the guest's
resolution. The web client reallocated its framebuffer but kept the canvas at the old size, so
part of the screen was cut off. The canvas now follows the reactivated size and the component's
canvas-resized callback (previously ignored) is called so it can rescale.

